#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:5
#: 403fe7f5e8be47608f5e653379bef74e
msgid "GPS - How it Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:7
#: 2e11a335d5b6413081015ba0e7ba293c
msgid "GPS system is a Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:12
#: a6a39dae12e94c388947c140763ec348
msgid "Most civil GPS receivers are using pseudorange data (C/A code) available on GPS L1 channel (1575.42 MHz) and optionally they can receive SBAS DGPS corrections giving meter precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:19
#: 826c8b91dcdf440d91fc4d0cce7dd9cb
msgid "Advanced and expensive civil GPS receivers can use the previous method plus carrier phase smoothing, carrier phase corrections (RTK) as well as L2 channel P(Y) code semi-codeless tracking (1227.60 MHz) for realtime local ionospheric corrections giving centimeter or even millimeter precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:28
#: b73b6cb444114cba83a557aac9d189b0
msgid "Some even more advanced GNSS receivers can combine DGPS and RTK corrections and can receive other GNSS satellite constellations (GLONASS, GALILEO, SBAS, Galileo, Beidou, IMES, QZSS, and/or NAVIC) and other channels (L2C, L5...) at the same time to enhance precision and fix reliability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:32
#: ceae00f561cf4b10b014b349098f9104
msgid "Military GPS receivers are able to decode the P(Y) code available on L1 and L2 channels giving ten times more precision in realtime compared to a pseudorange basic solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:37
#: 5fc6c1c3e6aa46f58552454db925ba37
msgid "GPS multipathing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:39
#: 0dda582bcfdd46edb07a8fa0af6dcc94
msgid "Multipathing is causing GPS position errors that are difficult to detect and compensate for. Multiple GNSS receivers are better suited to filter out multipathing thanks to a higher number of visible satellites at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:57
#: e3cf49d9708b4c0c9c049379e26e5afc
msgid "GPS disturbed signal propagation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:59
#: 44201e2958f240ecb8c9533080bc894d
msgid "Ionospheric perturbations and magnetic storms (solar activity) can cause signal delays. This can be partially compensated using SBAS and L1 / L2 decoding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:69
#: 171c4fdda6a44da68b8b433a8cd91ede
msgid "Decoding L1 and L2 channels at the same time do allow realtime ionospheric corrections through a differential technique. Unlike SBAS broadcasted ionospheric corrections, this method gives a better match to local ionospheric conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:77
#: 2ccbae473bc6428781dbad2ca3b6e9df
msgid "New channels (L2C, L5) for civil use will enhance signal acquisition and position precision as soon as new satellites constellations will be complete ( 2015 - 2020 )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:82
#: 791566d2762c48a1909068ee4586c931
msgid "GPS performance data for different scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:84
#: c0e893277a474a0c95914928fda0034d
msgid "Those values can be thought as a basis to understand GPS limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gps-how-it-works.rst:86
#: 6074649d617446cf88ddf2ab4afcec30
msgid "As a general rule only clear sky view is safe enough for Auto missions !"
msgstr ""

